            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44727",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "jupyter-server: Jupyter Server: Remote Code Execution via stored Cross-Site Scripting in nbconvert handlers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Jupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. Prior to 2.20, the nbconvert HTTP handlers in jupyter_server render user-authored notebook HTML under the Jupyter origin without a sandbox directive in their Content-Security-Policy. Combined with nbconvert.HTMLExporter's default non-sanitizing behavior, a notebook carrying an HTML payload in a display_data output triggers stored XSS with cookie access, full /api/* authority, and kernel RCE. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.20."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44727",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44727\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: jupyter_server\nFixed Version: 2.20.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-44727](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44727)\nJupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. Prior to 2.20, the nbconvert HTTP handlers in jupyter_server render user-authored notebook HTML under the Jupyter origin without a sandbox directive in their Content-Security-Policy. Combined with nbconvert.HTMLExporter's default non-sanitizing behavior, a notebook carrying an HTML payload in a display_data output triggers stored XSS with cookie access, full /api/* authority, and kernel RCE. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.20.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44727**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|jupyter_server|2.20.0|[CVE-2026-44727](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44727)|\n\nJupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. Prior to 2.20, the nbconvert HTTP handlers in jupyter_server render user-authored notebook HTML under the Jupyter origin without a sandbox directive in their Content-Security-Policy. Combined with nbconvert.HTMLExporter's default non-sanitizing behavior, a notebook carrying an HTML payload in a display_data output triggers stored XSS with cookie access, full /api/* authority, and kernel RCE. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.20."
              },
