            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61669",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "jupyter_server: Jupyter Server: Redirects to arbitrary external domains via insufficient validation of login parameter"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Jupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. In jupyter_server versions through 2.17.0, the next query parameter in the login flow is insufficiently validated in `LoginFormHandler._redirect_safe()`, which allows redirects to arbitrary external domains via values such as `///example.com`. An attacker can use a crafted login URL to redirect users to a malicious site and facilitate phishing attacks. This issue is fixed in version 2.18.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61669",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-61669\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: jupyter_server\nFixed Version: 2.18.0\nLink: [CVE-2025-61669](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61669)\nJupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. In jupyter_server versions through 2.17.0, the next query parameter in the login flow is insufficiently validated in `LoginFormHandler._redirect_safe()`, which allows redirects to arbitrary external domains via values such as `///example.com`. An attacker can use a crafted login URL to redirect users to a malicious site and facilitate phishing attacks. This issue is fixed in version 2.18.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-61669**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|jupyter_server|2.18.0|[CVE-2025-61669](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-61669)|\n\nJupyter Server is the backend for Jupyter web applications. In jupyter_server versions through 2.17.0, the next query parameter in the login flow is insufficiently validated in `LoginFormHandler._redirect_safe()`, which allows redirects to arbitrary external domains via values such as `///example.com`. An attacker can use a crafted login URL to redirect users to a malicious site and facilitate phishing attacks. This issue is fixed in version 2.18.0."
